--- b19 medium.en: Number five is your family, and the rules are very different depending on how the home passes on. If your children inherit it, their basis is its value when you die, so the profit built up before then is not taxed when they sell. But if you give them the home while you are alive, the IRS says that as a general rule, they take your basis. In Rayandana's case, the gift basis would be $200,000, not $900,000, and a child who never lived there may not get the exclusion.
