--- b20 medium.en: What should you do before you sign? One, count your dates, including the two-year window if you are a widow or widower. Two, gather your closing papers and improvement receipts. Three, estimate your gain with the free worksheets in Publication 523. Four, check what a gain would do to your Medicare premiums and Social Security tax. Five, the sale date is usually the closing date, so it decides which tax year the gain lands in.
