--- b21 medium.en: To sum up, 1. Owning and living in your home for 24 months within 5 years lets you exclude 250,000 or 500,000 jointly. 2. Gain is price minus costs minus basis, and improvements raise basis. 3. A taxable gain can lift your Medicare costs and the tax on your Social Security. 4. Partial and survivor rules change the limit. 5. An inherited home gets a new basis, while a gift usually keeps yours.
